title: The Captain
from: Captain Odile Marrow
gist: You told the Captain you're not sure yet. She'll ask you at the Line on Sunday, in front of everyone.
== lines
marrow: You've come about the letter. Go on. I'm listening.   [listen]
marrow > you: Not sure yet. That's honest. I'd rather have honest than quick.   [nod]
marrow: Then you have until Sunday. At the Line, after the oath, I'll ask you. In front of everyone, I'm afraid.
? choice
* In front of everyone?   flavour:share
  marrow: It's a ship. They'll have heard most of it already. Better from you.   [laugh]
* What would you do?   flavour:listen
  marrow: I was offered a desk once. I said no. I've never been sorry. That's me, though. Not you.
marrow: Talk to people. Zeke. Your friends. Your family. Then come and tell me. Carry on, {me}.
